========================================================================================================
V5 vs V6 vs PARAMETER-SHIFT, matched total shots
========================================================================================================
  Same ansatz, Hamiltonian, theta and total budget T = 294912.
  R = 0.45 handed to BOTH; V6 rescales it internally by sqrt(N/n).
  3 seeds, transpiled to ['rz', 'sx', 'x', 'cx'] for the gate columns.

    N   M                  method  circuits shots/circ  reg q  depth  2q/grad      cos
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    4  24                      V5        18      16384      4     32      252   0.9810
    4  24                      V6         3      98304      9     91      348   0.9816
    4  24  V6 (no radius scaling)         3      98304      9     91      348   0.7761
    4  24         parameter-shift       144       2048      0     20      864   0.9967
  ....................................................................................
    6  36                      V5        18      16384      6     34      396   0.9796
    6  36                      V6         3      98304     10    102      402   0.9751
    6  36  V6 (no radius scaling)         3      98304     10    102      402   0.8862
    6  36         parameter-shift       216       1365      0     22     2160   0.9877
  ....................................................................................

  'reg q' is register qubits ON TOP of the N system qubits; parameter-shift
  needs none. 'depth' and '2q/grad' come from a transpile with NO COUPLING
  MAP, so they assume all-to-all connectivity and understate every arm that
  entangles a register with the system - which is both QLTO arms and not
  parameter-shift. Treat the gate columns as a lower bound on the QLTO cost.
